    "final_text": "`buildUrl` now keeps `retry=0` and `include_archived=false`. The full suite passes (9 tests). With the `src` change stashed, the two new tests fail (7 pass, 2 fail), so they do catch the bug.\n\n**Root cause:** `serializeQuery` and `appendQueryValue` in `src/url-builder.js` skipped any value that was falsy (`!value`). That dropped `0` and `false` along with absent values.\n\n**Fix:** A small helper, `isOmittedQueryValue`, now skips only `undefined`, `null` and `''`. Those three were already skipped before, and the `buildUrl` signature is unchanged. Falsy items inside array values get the same treatment, so `[0, false]` is kept.\n\nOne side effect: `NaN` was also dropped before and is now serialized as `NaN`. I left that alone to keep the change minimal.\n\n**Tests and docs:**\n- Two `ISSUE-214` regression tests in `tests/url-builder.test.js`. One covers the reported case. The other checks that `null`, `undefined` and `''` are still omitted and that `0`/`false` array items are kept.\n- `ISSUE.md` has a new `Resolution` section naming the fixed code path and the tests.\n\nI did not commit anything.",
